{
  "requirement": "`Criterion::execute` can compute an answer without a configured model provider.\nA criterion can compute its answer directly using tracked inputs; deterministic\nexecution needs no configured agent.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has two obligations: `Criterion::execute` can compute an answer without a configured model provider, and a criterion can compute its answer directly from tracked inputs. Both are covered.\n\n- **No agent configured, computed answer:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent]` uses a `Memory` graph with no agent.\n  - It first asserts that `ctx.ask::<bool>()` fails with `ValidationError::NoAgentConfigured`. That shows no agent is available.\n  - It then runs `Validator::verify` on the deterministic `Review` criterion, which succeeds. `Review::execute` calls `ctx.read` on the node and returns `Assessment { result: false, rationale: text.0 }`.\n  - It asserts the computed result is false and the rationale is \"ordinary computation\".\n- **Tracked inputs:** the same test stores the evidence, loads it back, and asserts `saved.dependencies[0]` is a `Dependency::Node` whose fingerprint equals the text it read.\n- **Reinforcing tests:**\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly]` runs a deterministic criterion, so it needs no agent. It checks the outcome and the recorded dependencies and reads, and it checks reuse of the stored record.\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` computes typed answers deterministically. It checks the output, the empty dependencies and the execution counts.\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configured_agents_initialize_only_when_asked_and_report_setup_errors]` uses a configured provider whose credential is missing. A deterministic `Question(false, ..)` still completes with a dependency, and only the agent-asking `Question(true, ..)` fails. That shows deterministic execution does not touch the provider.\n\nI found no obligation or boundary the text names that these tests leave unchecked.",
